{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Completion evidence for the three previously unbanked repository-verifiable criteria:\n\n1. Numeric-consumer inventory (AC c07): a scoped search of tracked automation/deployment sources using `rg -n -i --glob \"*.yml\" --glob \"*.yaml\" --glob \"*.sh\" --glob \"*.py\" --glob \"*.service\" --glob \"*.timer\" --glob \"Jenkinsfile*\" \"(bridge|reconcil).{0,80}(3|4|75)|(3|4|75).{0,80}(bridge|reconcil)\" .github scripts infra` found no bridge/reconciler 3/4/75 handling in production workflows, scripts, probes, systemd units, or Jenkinsfiles. The remaining numeric-looking hits were unrelated issue ids, line/cadence comments, Jira priority probes, or Gerrit test-gate exit 3. `infra/systemd/rebar-autodeploy.service` and `.timer` contain no reconciler sentinel policy. The production workflow at `.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml:25-29` explicitly documents canonical preview/sync and 0/1/2. `tests/unit/workflow/test_reconcile_workflow_lint.py:181-193` executes the production run block for 0/1/2 and asserts the old case whitelist is absent. Compatibility-only 3/4/75 uses remain deliberately in `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py`, direct legacy tests, and documentation.\n\n2. Documentation (AC c08): `docs/exit-codes.md:29-54` defines canonical bridge 0/1/2, every benign state marker, retained legacy 3/4/75 translations, and the rolling-migration rationale. `docs/release-notes.md:29-46` records the same dual contract and states that systemd/Jenkins/scripts/checked-out workflows continue unchanged.\n\n3. Canonical constraint and continuity (AC c09): `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py:55-66` defines one typed disposition with separate canonical and legacy exits; `:68-87` returns `canonical_exit` only for preview/sync and `legacy_exit` otherwise. All canonical exits in the enum are 0/1/2, while only legacy fields carry 3/4/75. `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_reconcile_main.py`, `tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_cli_heldout.py`, and `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_lock_steal.py` exercise canonical and compatibility routes; the landed CI run 31300543302 passed the complete Python matrix. This is additive translation at the outer adapter, so old-vocabulary environments are not forced onto the new numeric contract."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786261395531856001,"uuid":"b50339b3-ba6c-4e1a-a2b7-4fe3cbe57c9e"}